    "success_criteria": {
      "criteria": [
        "When this repo has exactly one candidate -- a lane whose lane-state intent_id matches, whose status is running and current_phase is 2_spec or 3_implement, with an active-work entry for that intent whose phase equals current_phase (a bounded proxy for \"in progress\"; task_runs are never closed) -- and the given session_id has no session_bound event at all, `lane work check` prints one warning naming the session and the intent plus the command `lane work bind --intent=<id> --task-run=<id> --session-id=<session> --agent=<agent>`, and exits 0. The command is printed only when every id matches ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]*$ and running it from the check's own process cwd would resolve the same active-work file and spec dir as the candidate entry (asserted end-to-end by executing the printed command); otherwise the warning names the intent without a command. When the session is bound to a different task run (whether or not it is also bound to this one), a diagnostic is printed and no bind command is suggested (binding again would make the observation mixed); when it is bound only to this task run nothing is printed. Tests cover each branch.",
        "The session_id and agent can be given as flags or read from the hook JSON on stdin (Claude Code and Codex SessionStart payload `session_id`); with neither, or with malformed stdin, the command prints nothing and exits 0 (asserted by tests).",
        "With no lane at 2_spec or 3_implement, the command prints nothing; with two or more such lanes it names each candidate instead of guessing one; it never writes trace events, lane-state.json or any other file (asserted by a test comparing the spec dir and trace store before and after).",
        "Existing `lane work start|bind|run`, `lane validate`, `lane advance` and `lane calibrate` behavior and output are unchanged (existing tests stay green).",
        "All packages/* test suites, typecheck and biome stay green; CHANGELOG has an Unreleased entry and the README/docs show a SessionStart hook example for Claude Code and Codex."
      ],
      "recorded_at": "2026-11-20T10:59:34.205Z"
    }
  }
